# Toy-project shared UAT logins. This file is intentionally versioned so a
# fresh local clone gets the same sign-in passwords without manual setup.
# It contains no session, OIDC, worker, or Keycloak-admin secret, and not the
# mentor's own logins (mentor-analyst, mentor-leader), which stay in .env.uat.
#
# Sign-in account          Role(s)                                   Password line
# uat-briefing-analyst     Commercial Analyst (P1)                   UAT_PASSWORD_BRIEFING_ANALYST
# uat-briefing-director    Brand Director (P3)                       UAT_PASSWORD_BRIEFING_DIRECTOR
# uat-forecast-analyst     Commercial Analytics Analyst (CA)         UAT_PASSWORD_FORECAST_ANALYST
# uat-forecast-manager     Brand Manager (BM)                        UAT_PASSWORD_FORECAST_MANAGER
# uat-both-analyst         P1 + CA: both lanes, analyst view         UAT_PASSWORD_BOTH_ANALYST
# uat-both-leader          P3 + BM: both lanes, leadership view      UAT_PASSWORD_BOTH_LEADER
UAT_PASSWORD_FORECAST_ANALYST=UHzTdiSH0hPIHmnC
